<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>CLUEMD</title>
  <style>
    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
    }
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      background: #f4f8fb;
      color: #17202a;
    }
    header {
      padding: 22px 7%;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      background: white;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
    }
    .logo {
      font-size: 24px;
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: 1px;
    }
    nav a {
      text-decoration: none;
      color: #17202a;
      margin-left: 20px;
      font-weight: 600;
    }
    .hero {
      min-height: 80vh;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      text-align: center;
      padding: 60px 20px;
    }
    .hero-content {
      max-width: 750px;
    }
    .tag {
      font-size: 14px;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 2px;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    h1 {
      font-size: clamp(45px, 10vw, 80px);
      line-height: 1;
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }
    .hero p {
      font-size: 20px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin-bottom: 35px;
      color: #4b5563;
    }
    .button {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 16px 30px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      background: #17202a;
      color: white;
      text-decoration: none;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 17px;
    }
    .button:hover {
      opacity: 0.85;
    }
    .section {
      padding: 70px 7%;
      background: white;
    }
    .section h2 {
      text-align: center;
      font-size: 35px;
      margin-bottom: 15px;
    }
    .section-intro {
      text-align: center;
      max-width: 650px;
      margin: 0 auto 45px;
      color: #6b7280;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }
    .steps {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: 20px;
      max-width: 1000px;
      margin: auto;
    }
    .step {
      padding: 30px;
      border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
      border-radius: 18px;
      background: #fafafa;
    }
    .step-number {
      font-size: 14px;
      font-weight: 800;
      margin-bottom: 15px;
    }
    .step h3 {
      margin-bottom: 10px;
      font-size: 21px;
    }
    .step p {
      color: #6b7280;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }
    footer {
      padding: 30px 7%;
      text-align: center;
      background: #17202a;
      color: white;
      font-size: 13px;
    }
    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .steps {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
      nav {
        display: none;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<header>
  <div class="logo">MEDMYSTERY</div>
  <nav>
    <a href="#how">How It Works</a>
    <a href="#about">About</a>
  </nav>
</header>
<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-content">
<div class="tag">Interactive Science Learning</div>
<h1>Can you solve the mystery?</h1>
<p>
  Investigate fictional cases, ask questions, collect clues,
  and use your biology knowledge to uncover the answer.
</p>
<a href="#how" class="button">Start a Mystery</a>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section" id="how">
  <h2>How It Works</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    MEDMYSTERY transforms biology from something students memorize
    into something they investigate.
  </p>
  <div class="steps">
<div class="step">
  <div class="step-number">01</div>
  <h3>Investigate</h3>
  <p>
    Meet a fictional character and ask questions to uncover
    important clues.
  </p>
</div>
<div class="step">
  <div class="step-number">02</div>
  <h3>Think</h3>
  <p>
    Connect the information you discover and use scientific
    reasoning to form a hypothesis.
  </p>
</div>
<div class="step">
  <div class="step-number">03</div>
  <h3>Solve</h3>
  <p>
    Submit your answer and discover the science behind the mystery.
  </p>
</div>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section" id="about">
  <h2>Why MEDMYSTERY?</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    Students often learn biology by memorizing information.
    MEDMYSTERY gives them a place to actually use what they know,
    ask their own questions, and develop scientific reasoning
    through fictional interactive cases.
  </p>
</section>
<footer>
  MEDMYSTERY · A fictional educational science experience
</footer>
</body>
</html>
